01:00:33,333 --> 01:00:39,333
Olivia Haigh Williams (born 26 July 1968) is an English actress who
appears in British and American films and television.

11
01:06:36,666 --> 01:06:42,666
Williams studied drama at the Bristol Old Vic Theatre School for two years
followed by three years at the Royal Shakespeare Company.

12
01:12:40,000 --> 01:12:46,000
Her first significant screen role was as Jane Fairfax in the British
television film Emma (1996), based on Jane Austen's novel.

13
01:18:43,333 --> 01:18:49,333
She made her film debut in 1997's The Postman, followed by
Rushmore (1998) and The Sixth Sense (1999).

14
01:24:46,666 --> 01:24:52,666
Williams also acted in the British films Lucky Break (2001),
The Heart of Me (2002) and An Education (2009).

15
01:30:50,000 --> 01:30:56,000
She continued acting in films such as The Ghost Writer (2010), Hanna (2011), Anna Karenina (2012), Hyde Park on
Hudson (2012), Sabotage (2014), Maps to the Stars (2014), Victoria & Abdul (2017), and The Father (2020).

16
01:36:53,333 --> 01:36:59,333
From 2017 to 2019, she played Emily Silk in the science
fiction television series Counterpart.

17
01:42:56,666 --> 01:43:02,666
From 2022 to 2023, Williams portrayed Queen Camilla in Netflix's
historical drama The Crown in its final two seasons.
